    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F52" sourceRef="T31" targetRef="End1" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Anno_Legend">
      <bpmn:text>Legend - green circle: Start Event | red circle: End Event | purple rounded box: action performed by a person (Guest or SRS Author) | white rounded box: action performed automatically by the system | diamond with X: Exclusive Gateway (decision) | circle on the edge of a task: boundary timer event | box with + : collapsed sub-process | solid arrow: Sequence Flow (inside one pool) | dashed arrow: Message Flow (between two pools) | box with folded corner: Text Annotation (business rule).</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Anno_Meter">
      <bpmn:text>BR-01 Credit metering: every call to the LLM Provider (steps 6, 8, 16, 18, 20, 22, 26, 29, and step 24 when the author asks for an AI priority suggestion) meters token consumption and deducts credits, and the balance is checked before each call. The gateway "Sufficient credits?" models this check at the single point where an insufficient balance blocks the flow.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Anno_Boundary">
      <bpmn:text>System boundary: the AI Business Analyst capability is part of FlintFlow and lives in the "FlintFlow System" lane. Only model inference, e-mail delivery and card processing are bought from vendors, so those three appear as black-box pools. They are infrastructure participants, not use-case actors - the actors are Guest, SRS Author, Admin and Payment Gateway.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Anno_AIFail">
      <bpmn:text>BR-02 AI failure handling: the event sub-process is triggered by an AI error or timeout raised by any generation step (16, 18, 20, 22). Content already accepted by the author is preserved; the interrupted step is re-run as a new process instance, it does not resume the token that was cancelled.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Anno_Baseline">
      <bpmn:text>BR-03 SRS baseline: accepting an artifact in steps 17/19/21/23 only adds it to the Working Draft. The document becomes an approved SRS Baseline (v1.0) at step 30, which is a precondition for the exports in step 31. After the baseline exists, any material change follows Change Baselined Requirement (impact analysis - review - approval - new version).</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
  </bpmn:process>
